    xt_legend: 'Extra: DAE, Midi, A-A',
    // Info & Macros tab
    info_credits_title: 'Credits, licenses and privacy',
    info_credits_html: '<ul><li><b>Unofficial tool.</b> Tafy\'s Actor Forge is not affiliated with or endorsed by Foundry Gaming LLC, Wizards of the Coast or the authors of the modules mentioned. Foundry Virtual Tabletop and Dungeons &amp; Dragons are trademarks of their respective owners. The Forge makes fifth edition compatible (5E compatible) content for Foundry\'s dnd5e system.</li><li><b>Spells (SRD).</b> To link monster spells the Forge contains the names, levels and ids of the spells in the dnd5e system compendiums. <i>This work includes material taken from the System Reference Document 5.1 (“SRD 5.1”) by Wizards of the Coast LLC and available at <a href="https://dnd.wizards.com/resources/systems-reference-document" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://dnd.wizards.com/resources/systems-reference-document</a>. The SRD 5.1 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License available at <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode</a>.</i> <i>This work includes material from the System Reference Document 5.2.1 (“SRD 5.2.1”) by Wizards of the Coast LLC, available at <a href="https://www.dndbeyond.com/srd" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://www.dndbeyond.com/srd</a>. The SRD 5.2.1 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, available at <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode</a>.</i></li><li><b>JB2A animations.</b> Previews and paths in the Animations section come from <a href="https://github.com/Jules-Bens-Aa/JB2A_DnD5e" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JB2A — Jules&amp;Ben\'s Animated Assets</a> (free library), licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. The videos are not included in the Forge: previews load from JB2A\'s GitHub repository. The list of paths is taken from the JB2A module and shared under the same license. To use the animations in Foundry you need the JB2A and Automated Animations modules.</li><li><b>Supported modules.</b> The JSON it makes uses dnd5e, Midi-QOL, DAE and Automated Animations data: the Forge contains none of their code.</li><li><b>Privacy.</b> Everything runs in your browser: no account, no Forge server, no data collected. Drafts and collection stay in this browser only (localStorage). The only external requests are the JB2A previews (GitHub).</li></ul>',
    info_how_title: 'How to use', info_bye: '⚔️ Happy prepping, and may your dice always roll in your favor!',
    info_how_html: '<p>Fill in the sheet fields (<b>Monster</b>, <b>Item</b> or <b>Spell</b>): the JSON preview updates live. When ready, press <b>Export</b> to download the file, or <b>Add to collection</b> to gather many into one file.</p><p>To import into Foundry, copy the <b>importer macro</b> once (below or from the button on the sheet), paste it into a <i>Script</i> macro, then paste the JSON there: Actors, Items and Spells are sorted and created automatically, even inside a compendium. From its <b>Export</b> tab the same macro saves a whole folder (e.g. the party) or a compendium into one file, or a zip with one file per document: re-import it elsewhere or load it here in the <b>Encounter</b> tab.</p><p>Optional fields (DAE effects, A-A animations, Midi macros) live in the <b>Extra</b> menu, collapsed until you need them.</p>',
    info_tips_title: 'Quick tips',
    info_tips_html: '<ul><li>Images must end in .webp/.png/.jpg; external URLs show on the sheet but often not on the map (CORS): better to upload them to the server.</li><li>For damage use English ids: <code>2d8 + @mod piercing, 8d8 fire</code>.</li><li>A-A animations search the <b>free</b> JB2A library paths (short forms: “slash”, “claw”, “fireball”).</li><li>Always review the sheet before exporting: the tools speed you up, the check is yours.</li></ul>',
    info_macros_title: '🎲 Useful macros', info_macros_hint: 'Copy the code, paste it into a Foundry <i>Script</i> macro and tweak the CONFIG block at the top. Every macro (Import / Export included) speaks the language set in Foundry: Italian or English.', info_copy: 'Copy',
    mp_importer: 'Import / Export (main macro)', mp_importer_desc: 'Two tabs. Import: paste the JSON or pick several files, into the world or a compendium; it recognises Actors, Items, Spells, Journals, Scenes, Tables and rebuilds subfolders. Export: pick the source (Actors, Items, Journals, Scenes… or a compendium) and the folder, then a single JSON file (to re-import or load here in the Encounter tab) or a zip with one file per document.',
    mp_cinematic: 'Cinematic scene', mp_cinematic_desc: 'Shows a fullscreen image and starts a playlist track at the same instant, preloading both to avoid hitches.',
    mp_transform: 'Token transformation', mp_transform_desc: 'Swaps the selected token for another form (optional sound + animation). Re-running it restores the original token and stops the animation.',
    mp_groupsave: 'Group saving throw', mp_groupsave_desc: 'All selected tokens roll the same save against a DC; the result with ✅/❌ appears in chat.',
    mp_condition: 'Condition on selected', mp_condition_desc: 'Applies or removes a condition (prone, poisoned, frightened…) on all selected tokens with one click.',
    mp_massdamage: 'Mass damage / heal', mp_massdamage_desc: 'Asks for an amount and applies it as damage or healing to all selected tokens at once.',
